"The real Princess Sylthaeryn is dead; she used the Order on her bonded slime to be killed."
"The princess now seen in Keld is a persona of that slime, Syl, who bears Sylthaeryn's looks."
"Loreleia knows her daughter is dead and took on heavy debt to help the slime escape."
"Syl holds a true Branch Head Emblem, so she speaks for the Feirelle branch in all but name."
"Keldenar's royal protection of Sylthaeryn is bait to lure out Dornhallow and Outeatus agents."
"The Dornhallows killed their own tree spirit, most likely by a necromantic ritual."
"Keldenar was reborn from another world and is bound by oath not to harm or expose Syl."
"The slime Syl was once a human noble prodigy, poisoned by his older brother."
"That brother poisoned him with cake on his birthday, jealous of his legacy dimension magic."
"The great spirit of Caelthal can question tree spirits, a taboo used only once before."
"Mermen kings and queens do not spawn naturally, so the Vaelyssan mermen may never recover."
"Ruling a kingdom is one of three ways to join the order of the world: rule, dungeon, or godhood."
